commit.message:
Use fallback in attr() for outer cycles

Use fallback value for outer cycles in attr, for example:

data-foo=attr(data-foo type(<length>), 3px);
--x: attr(data-foo type(<length>), 11px);

--x should fallback to `11px`.

If current property is in the cycle, we don't use fallback, i.e.:

data-foo=var(--x, 3px);
--x: attr(data-foo type(<length>), 11px);

here --x is iacvt.

More info in tests to this CL.

Fixed: 440287244
